{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3902","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3902","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3902\",\"parent_revision\":\"255e5862244df04ea9864674d52e6aff4f388549bfabb8c163ea02b697bac975\",\"root_revision\":\"255e5862244df04ea9864674d52e6aff4f388549bfabb8c163ea02b697bac975\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nDetermine whether retaining immutable evidence of the inputs actually supplied to a DH execution attempt would materially improve failure diagnosis and baseline-versus-candidate evaluation, without imposing disproportionate storage, privacy, context, or launch overhead.\\n\\nThis is a research-first integration evaluation, not a requirement to install Oh My Subagents (OMS), adopt its architecture, or ship a new context store. An evidence-backed decision to adopt, adapt, reject, or remain inconclusive is the deliverable.\\n\\n**OBSERVED \u2014 current DH contract:** At `9dc96e51be1f277345207c8d9664c17ecda2b095`, the work-loop procedure launches a runner with a logical task address, attempt number, and specialist profile, keeps launch-handle associations in working notes, and settles returned text before adjudication. These are existing capabilities to preserve. This inspection does not establish everything each supported harness already records about effective instructions or later context loading.\\n\\n**OBSERVED \u2014 external prior art:** OMS distinguishes an immutable Assignment, its execution Attempt, and each Dispatch. Its runtime contract stores the exact resolved instruction/input strings per Dispatch, reuses them for a restart of that Dispatch, and supplies a new typed continuation for later turns. That is a candidate pattern, not evidence that DH needs the same record model or that it improves DH outcomes.\\n\\n**Hypothesis**: Preserving the supplied dispatch inputs and their relevant revision/environment provenance at an existing DH execution boundary makes instruction-sensitive failures and comparative skill evaluations more reproducible and diagnosable than the evidence available today, with a worthwhile cost trade-off.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] The existing per-harness evidence inventory and unresolved visibility boundaries are documented with source or execution evidence; absence is not inferred solely from the work-loop prose.\\n- [ ] The hypothesis is evaluated against the existing behavior, or a precise capability/authority blocker is recorded without fabricating execution or benefit.\\n- [ ] Any candidate preserves DH's canonical backend, attempt identity, authority checks, readiness-based scheduling, independent verification and completion semantics. No second scheduler or orchestration state machine is introduced by this evaluation.\\n- [ ] Evaluation records explain how historical inputs remain distinguishable after skills, profiles or referenced content change, and what cannot be reconstructed. Capture failures cannot silently become successful evidence or accepted work.\\n- [ ] An adopt/adapt/reject/inconclusive decision states demonstrated benefits, costs, privacy implications and remaining uncertainty. Shipping the candidate is not required for completion; inconclusive evidence does not change production defaults.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a DH maintainer comparing an original skill with a candidate or investigating an interrupted attempt, I need to distinguish changes in the instructions and inputs actually used from changes in the skill's behavior, so that I do not misdiagnose failures or accept an invalid comparison.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Agent task - auto-derived from input; user requested an evaluation-worthy integration following the OMS comparison.\\n- **Priority**: P2 \u2014 exploratory candidate with no demonstrated DH improvement yet.\\n- **Type**: Feature, research-first.\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-25.\\n- **Creation classification**: BEHAVIORAL/PROCESS; the evaluation behavior and protected contracts are the requirement, not a prescribed schema or implementation.\\n- **Duplicate check**: Searched immutable dispatch, dispatch context, DispatchRequest, attempt reproducibility and dispatch/reproducibility. No equivalent standalone evaluation item was identified. #931 concerns restoring milestone coordination after compaction; #3223/#3689 concern workflow-graph extraction/publication; #1091/#1092 concern session reuse and context headroom. None establishes this per-attempt supplied-input evidence decision.\\n- **Related**: #3123 is a worktree/source-identity failure example, not evidence that this candidate fixes that bug. #3901 is the separate, smaller current handoff correction and is not a dependency for research.\\n- **Workflow stage**: Captured for grooming; no experiment or integration has been executed. Created through GitHub MCP because the DH backlog_add endpoint is not exposed in this session.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Research First\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n1. Establish the present evidence boundary for the relevant DH launch paths and supported harnesses. Which supplied prompts, loaded profiles/skills, revisions, worktree identities, settings, and continuation inputs are already recoverable? Distinguish directly observed content, retained references, inferred content, and inaccessible provider-managed context. Do not claim that saving a launch prompt captures all later tool reads or hidden provider instructions.\\n2. Determine the smallest genuinely missing evidence, if any. Compare using existing task/attempt records and harness traces with the OMS-inspired capture pattern. Existing records that already answer the question should be reused, not duplicated.\\n3. Before judging a candidate, declare the evaluation cases, protected behavior, meaningful benefit, and decision rule. Include unchanged inputs, a skill/profile changing between attempts, continuation after interruption, a mutable or missing referenced file, and unavailable capture. Use comparable baseline/candidate conditions, isolated repetitions and held-out cases where practical; report unsupported harness paths rather than generalizing.\\n4. Assess whether an independent evaluator can establish the actual supplied instruction/input revision and correctly distinguish input drift from a behavioral defect. Record capture completeness, diagnostic accuracy, storage growth, context cost, tool calls and elapsed overhead separately. No aggregate quality score and no invented numerical acceptance threshold.\\n5. Evaluate redaction, access, retention, deletion and interruption behavior before any persistent sensitive-data capture. Use non-sensitive evaluation fixtures. A reference or digest alone must not be represented as preserved readable content; redacted or unavailable content must not be called an exact replay. Reproducing inputs does not promise deterministic model outputs.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Evidence\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [DH work loop at the inspected revision](https://github.com/Jamie-BitFlight/claude_skills/blob/9dc96e51be1f277345207c8d9664c17ecda2b095/plugins/development-harness/docs/work-ledger/work-loop.md).\\n- [OMS runtime: Assignment, Attempt, Dispatch and stored requests, pinned to fcc4398](https://github.com/ringlochid/oh-my-subagents/blob/fcc439858f73fe51dfa9a39ecb89155965488f1b/docs-internal/architecture/runtime.md).\\n- [OMS prompt composition and exact DispatchRequest contract at the same revision](https://github.com/ringlochid/oh-my-subagents/blob/fcc439858f73fe51dfa9a39ecb89155965488f1b/docs-internal/architecture/system-prompts.md).\\n\\n**User-provided context**: The preceding assessment proposed investigating exact effective dispatch-context capture at DH's existing launch boundary rather than introducing OMS as a second runtime. Treat that as the candidate to evaluate, not an approved implementation design.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"ba94f6c22e6298a4faeee7173de8ee2774010535dea803d522cd27570e238346\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABXCLVog\"}"}